Permission49210004=Send membership applications through the API: members in draft with consents
VereineSetupTabConsents=Consents
VereineConsentHowToWhy=<strong>What for:</strong> some things need a consent, for example photos on the website or the newsletter. The association must be able to show that someone agreed and to what (Art. 7 (1) GDPR).
VereineConsentHowToVersion=<strong>Version:</strong> every text has a version. Changing text or label creates a new version; earlier consents keep the version agreed to.
VereineConsentHowToWithdraw=<strong>Withdrawal:</strong> a consent can be withdrawn at any time, as easily as it was given (Art. 7 (3) GDPR). The member's tab <em>Association</em> keeps the whole history.
VereineConsentHowToWebsite=<strong>Website:</strong> it reads the texts with <code>GET /vereine/consents</code> and sends a membership application with the consents given to <code>POST /vereine/applications</code>. That creates a member in draft, which the association checks and validates.
VereineConsentHowToChildren=<strong>Children:</strong> for online services offered directly to children, a child in Austria can consent itself from the age of 14 (§ 4 (4) DSG); younger children need their parents.
